INT. EMERGENCY ROOM - TRAUMA BAY THREE - NIGHT

Blood on the floor. Monitors shrieking. A gurney with a young man strapped to it, chest rising in shallow gasps.

DR. CHIDINMA OKAFOR-LINDQVIST, 40s, in a gown and gloves, leans over the patient. Beside her, RESIDENT DR. CYRUS ACHTERBERG-NNAMDI, 20s, holds a suction wand, white-faced. At the foot of the bed, NURSE BEATRIZ COLQUHOUN-SANTOS, 30s, cuts the patient's shirt with trauma shears.

CHIDINMA
Pressure?

CYRUS
Seventy over forty.

BEATRIZ
Falling.

CHIDINMA
Two large-bore lines. Now.

CYRUS
Already in.

BEATRIZ
Left arm's blown.

CHIDINMA
Then go to the neck.

CYRUS
Dr. Okafor-Lindqvist, he's seventeen.

CHIDINMA
Pressure.

BEATRIZ
Sixty over thirty.

CYRUS
What's the mechanism?

CHIDINMA
Stab wound, left chest, no exit.

BEATRIZ
Pulse ox ninety.

CYRUS
Pneumothorax?

CHIDINMA
Hemothorax. Chest tube. Cyrus, you do it.

CYRUS
Me?

CHIDINMA
Yes. Now.

BEATRIZ
Betadine.

CYRUS
Okay. Okay.

CHIDINMA
Fifth intercostal, mid-axillary. You know this.

CYRUS
I know this.

BEATRIZ
Pressure's fifty.

CHIDINMA
Push the blood.

BEATRIZ
O-neg's up.

CYRUS
Incision.

CHIDINMA
Good. Bluntly through the muscle.

CYRUS
There's a rush of blood.

CHIDINMA
Good. That's the chest. Insert the tube.

CYRUS
It's in.

BEATRIZ
Pressure sixty.

CHIDINMA
Seventy?

BEATRIZ
Seventy.

CYRUS
Output is eight hundred cc and rising.

CHIDINMA
We go to the OR.

BEATRIZ
OR's clearing.

CHIDINMA
Get the surgeon.

BEATRIZ
Calling.

CYRUS
Dr. Okafor-Lindqvist?

CHIDINMA
Yes?

CYRUS
I thought he was gone.

CHIDINMA
So did I.

She rips off her gloves. Squeezes his shoulder once.

CHIDINMA (CONT'D)
Good work, Doctor.
